{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Imprint — extdir{% endblock %}
{% block meta_description %}Legal notice (Impressum) for extdir, as required by § 5 DDG.{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
<div class="wrap page">
    <div class="page-head">
        <h1>Imprint</h1>
        <p>
            Angaben gemäß § 5 DDG (Digitale-Dienste-Gesetz) und § 18 Abs. 2 MStV.
            Legal notice for a site operated from Germany.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
        <h2>Operator</h2>
        <address>
            {{ operator.name }}<br>
            {{ operator.street }}<br>
            {{ operator.postalCity }}<br>
            {{ operator.country }}
        </address>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
            Email: <a href="mailto:{{ operator.email }}">{{ operator.email }}</a>
        </p>
        <p class="small">
            Email is the fastest route and is monitored. No telephone number is published:
            § 5 DDG does not require one where an email address and a further means of fast,
            direct contact are available.
        </p>

        <h2>Responsible for content (§ 18 Abs. 2 MStV)</h2>
        <p>{{ operator.name }}, address as above.</p>

        <h2>Legal status</h2>
        <p>
            extdir is operated by a private individual as a non-commercial community project.
            There is no company behind it, no revenue, no advertising and nothing for sale.
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Commercial register:</strong> not registered. There is no legal entity to register.</li>
            <li><strong>VAT identification number:</strong> none issued (§ 5 Abs. 1 Nr. 6 DDG applies only where one exists).</li>
            <li><strong>Regulated profession:</strong> not applicable. Software development is not a chambered profession in Germany.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Not affiliated with Shopware AG</h2>
        <p>
            extdir is an independent community project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by,
            sponsored by or connected to Shopware AG in any way. The name “Shopware” is used
            descriptively, to identify the software these extensions are written for. All
            trademarks are the property of their respective owners.
        </p>

        <h2>Liability for content</h2>
        <p>
            As a service provider, the operator is responsible for their own content on these pages
            under general law (§ 7 Abs. 1 DDG). Under §§ 8 to 10 DDG, however, the operator is not
            obliged to monitor transmitted or stored third-party information, or to investigate
            circumstances indicating unlawful activity. Obligations to remove or block the use of
            information under general law remain unaffected.
        </p>
        <p>
            The extension entries on this site are generated automatically from publicly published
            package metadata. They describe third-party software that the operator neither wrote nor
            controls.
        </p>

        <h2>Liability for links</h2>
        <p>
            This site links extensively to external repositories and package pages whose content the
            operator has no influence over. No liability can be accepted for that content; the
            respective provider or operator of the linked pages is always responsible for it. Linked
            pages were checked for obvious legal violations at the time of linking. Permanent
            monitoring of linked content is not reasonable without concrete evidence of an
            infringement. On becoming aware of infringements, such links will be removed promptly.
        </p>

        <h2>Copyright</h2>
        <p>
            Extension names, descriptions and logos belong to their respective authors and are
            reproduced here as factual reference. Each indexed extension remains under its own
            licence, which is shown on its page. If you believe something here infringes your rights,
            the <a href="{{ path('takedown') }}">takedown policy</a> explains how to have it removed.
        </p>

        <h2>Consumer dispute resolution</h2>
        <p>
            The operator is neither obliged nor willing to participate in dispute resolution
            proceedings before a consumer arbitration board.
        </p>

        <p class="small subtle" style="margin-top:2rem">
            Last updated: {{ 'now'|date('Y-m-d') }} ·
            <a href="{{ path('privacy') }}">Privacy</a> ·
            <a href="{{ path('terms') }}">Terms</a> ·
            <a href="{{ path('takedown') }}">Takedown policy</a>
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
